      "message": "Great job on the coverage improvements. \n\nUnfortunately 5 executions / sec is extremely low for fuzzing. Can you please take a look at the Expensive Initialization docs (especially `LLVMFuzzerInitialize`):\n\nIf the library you are testing requires some expensive/slow initialization you should consider moving that code into a separate LLVMFuzzerInitialize() function. This function will be called once, when the fuzz target starts. The code in LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput() is then called repeatedly in a loop.\n\n\nMore here: go/fuzzer-review-checklist",
